#{[17592186557236 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557236 #edb/ref 1069 "q-89991" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557236 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557236 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the root of $f(x)=\\sqrt{3x+1}+4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557236 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3b5454cb-d7d1-50b2-8aa5-cfa1e1b3686a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557236 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3x+1}+4=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3x+1}+4 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3x+1} & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any solutions since its left-hand side is always nonnegative, while the right-hand side is negative.\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has no roots." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557248 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557142 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557248 #edb/ref 1069 "q-115385" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557248 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557248 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the range of $f(x)=3\\sqrt{5x+9}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557248 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4cbeb52a-0392-5f34-918d-f2e44920e406" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557248 #edb/ref 1074 "The range of $\\sqrt{x}$ is\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{x}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches do not affect the range. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{5x+9}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5x+9} & \\ge 0 \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5x+9} & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range of the given function is $f(x)\\in [0,\\infty ).$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/8e/8ece70a3c8855e00a0232248cb922a40c8c9756ef67ea12b012eb719c8ee3bd1.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557276 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557165 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557276 #edb/ref 1069 "q-115388" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557276 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557276 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the root of $f(x)=2\\sqrt{5x+10}+3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557276 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "821416d3-f1f2-5d6c-b79b-722f962867ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557276 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{5x+10}+3=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{5x+10}+3 & =0 \\\\ 2\\sqrt{5x+10} & =-3 \\\\ \\sqrt{5x+10} & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any solutions since its left-hand side is always nonnegative, while the right-hand side is negative.\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has no roots." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557288 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557199 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557288 #edb/ref 1069 "q-115372" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557288 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557288 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the domain of $f(x)=5\\sqrt{4x-3}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557288 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9e99c86a-1348-545b-9c9f-3a1428e5141e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557288 #edb/ref 1074 "The domain of $y=\\sqrt{x}$ is\n\n$$\nx\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nTo find the domain of $f(x)=5\\sqrt{4x-3},$ we replace $x$ with $4x-3$ in the above inequality. This gives\n\n$$\n4x-3\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nSolving this inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-3 & \\ge 0 \\\\ 4x & \\ge 3 \\\\ x & \\ge \\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $y=f(x)$ is $x\\in [\\frac{3}{4},\\infty ).$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/f7/f71e9e717ab5c217d91528de89540de9013eadd31b1907c89d43d589fb6929af.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557292 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557292 #edb/ref 1069 "q-115377" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557292 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557292 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the domain of $f(x)=3\\sqrt{8x}-2?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557292 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "acd7fcaf-37e0-5893-ba70-06ebe65a32f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557292 #edb/ref 1074 "The domain of $y=\\sqrt{x}$ is\n\n$$\nx\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nTo find the domain of $f(x)=3\\sqrt{8x}-2,$ we replace $x$ with $8x$ in the above inequality. This gives\n\n$$\n8x\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nSolving this inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x & \\ge 0 \\\\ x & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $y=f(x)$ is $x\\in [0,\\infty ).$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/ef/efbc925cd1aca7f476d6cfc11f3c668c4f3bde78acf359eb0a65696ce2a12852.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557297 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557146 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557297 #edb/ref 1069 "q-277380" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557297 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557297 #edb/ref 1071 "The root of the function $f(x)=-\\sqrt{8-2x}+4$ is $x=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557297 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "be201399-7461-56d1-865b-23d766571416" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557297 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n-\\sqrt{8-2x}+4=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{8-2x}+4 & =0 \\\\ -\\sqrt{8-2x} & =-4 \\\\ \\sqrt{8-2x} & =4 \\\\ (\\sqrt{8-2x})^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ 8-2x & =16 \\\\ -2x & =8 \\\\ x & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we must check the answer by substituting it back into the initial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{8-2(-4)}+4 & =0 \\\\ -\\sqrt{8+8}+4 & =0 \\\\ -\\sqrt{16}+4 & =0 \\\\ -4+4 & =0 \\\\ -4+4 & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=-4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557304 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557133 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557304 #edb/ref 1069 "q-89992" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557304 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557304 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the root of $f(x)=\\sqrt{4-5x}+10.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557304 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c6dd5656-22b2-5e5b-b391-f41ec70a470b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557304 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{4-5x}+10=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{4-5x}+10 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt{4-5x} & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any solutions since its left-hand side is always nonnegative, while the right-hand side is negative.\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has no roots." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557315 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557068 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557315 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186557164 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557315 #edb/ref 1069 "q-277275" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557315 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557315 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the domain of $f(x)=\\sqrt{6x-5}.$\n\nThe domain is $x\\in [${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557315 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ddedbc01-5d9e-5e7a-be28-fa7766a765e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186557315 #edb/ref 1074 "The domain of $y=\\sqrt{x}$ is\n\n$$\nx\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nTo find the domain of $f(x)=\\sqrt{6x-5},$ we replace $x$ with $6x-5$ in the above inequality. This gives\n\n$$\n6x-5\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nSolving this inequality, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-5 & \\ge 0 \\\\ 6x & \\ge 5 \\\\ x & \\ge \\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $y=f(x)$ is $x\\in [\\frac{5}{6},\\infty ).$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/4d/4d0a6205a61aa0625a082d6d3bc1941ab00e0536c85844f28af873798bf6db64.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
